Add missing <cassert> includes to fcl headers.

16 installed fcl headers call assert() but none include <cassert>;
they relied on transitive includes. GCC 15 / libstdc++ in Fedora 44 no
longer pull <cassert> in transitively, so both fcl's own build and every
downstream consumer of fcl-devel (e.g. DART) fail to compile. Add the
include directly after each header's include guard.

Upstream: not yet reported; trivially correct.

